# Yarus, Roar of the Old Gods: a returned card that can't be turned face up stays face down (the ruling): a 2/2 with no name,
# mana cost or creature types, and no ward {2}, since it was neither disguised nor cloaked (CR 708.2a, 702.168a). Turn 1 Bot1
# casts Yarus and Vengeful Creeper face down. Turn 2 Bot2 casts Karlov Watchdog ("Permanents your opponents control can't be
# turned face up during your turn"), then Lightning Bolt at the face-down Creeper, which has ward {2} (the Bolt and the ward
# trigger on the stack), paying it. Yarus returns the Creeper face down and can't turn it up: it stays a face-down 2/2 with only
# the haste Yarus gives, and Bot1 still knows it. Turn 4 Bot2 bolts it again and no ward triggers: it dies and comes back once
# more, still face down.

